\"]))`, and it should subtract 1 from the day number. Every ordinal date is shifted by one day, including ordinals inside datetimes, such as `2004-060T20:23:19Z`.\n\nI kept those tests failing rather than marking them `xfail` or deleting them, because they are the tests that catch this bug. Once the line is fixed, all 12 should pass. If you need a green run before the fix, tell me and I'll mark them `xfail`.\n\nThe tests cover date, time, datetime, timezone and duration parsing and formatting, `strftime` formats, and `Duration` arithmetic, equality and `totimedelta`.\n\nWhile writing them I found a few library quirks that I left out because they look like upstream behaviour rather than bugs. `PT` and `P1DT` parse without error, and the alternative duration format fails with a `ValueError` for year or month 0. I also dropped one test of my own that was ill-defined (ordinal day `000`).\n\nThe untracked `isodate/__pycache__/` directory comes from running the tests.","ttft_ms":2436,"type":"result","duration_ms":105503,"uuid":"442f4541-931a-4338-9957-57b522278e22","ttft_stream_ms":1356,"time_to_request_ms":242,"first_content_frame_ms":1356,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
